---
title: "The Clay Lesson"
note: "Improper Bodies: a lump of clay spreads on its second fall, and the body of VICTIM loses its firmness and keeps every impression, conscious the whole time. From Codie's tested prompt. VICTIM is your ref image 1; delete (image 1) for text only."
tags: [curator, h3, body_horror, ito]
---
@h3 ref2va 16:9 lite
style: live-action, cinematic surreal body horror, photorealistic
$curator = __curator__
$victim = __bh_victim__
$room = __bh_room__
$touch = {shoulder|upper arm|chest}

CAST
CURATOR: $curator
VICTIM (image 1): $victim

SHOT 10s | push in, small, slow
VICTIM stands facing CURATOR in $room, a small lump of grey clay on a table nearby. CURATOR lets the clay fall once; it lands unchanged.
CURATOR (soft, polite voice): __curator_line__
CURATOR rolls it between long fingers, murmurs quietly and drops it again; this time it lands and spreads into a soft flattened mass. CURATOR places one hand gently on the $touch of VICTIM, and the body begins losing its firmness: the shoulder caves inward under its own weight, followed by the upper arm and chest. Wherever VICTIM grips themself, deep dents remain, and one cheek sags and only partly recovers. The torso slumps downward, soft and moldable, still recognizably human. In the final moment CURATOR steps forward and presses a thumb gently into the forehead of VICTIM, leaving a deep, perfect indentation.
SFX: quiet indoor ambience; soft footsteps; distressed breathing; thick, soft pressure sounds as the body keeps every impression
MUSIC: N/A
